---
// versioning, and CHANGELOG.md from the repository root, rendered as it is.
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { Content as Changelog, getHeadings } from '../../../../CHANGELOG.md';
import { url } from '../../data/site';

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'versioning', text: 'versioning' },
  ...getHeadings(),
];
---
<Doc
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'versioning & changelog',
    description: 'What a version of the nalet design system promises, and every change so far.',
  }}
  headings={headings}
>
  <h1>versioning & changelog</h1>
  <p>What a version number promises, and the changelog of every release.</p>
  <h2 id="versioning">versioning</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Semantic versions.</strong> While the system is 0.x, a minor version (0.3.0) may change how existing
      components look — the changelog lists every visible change; a patch (0.3.1) only fixes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>One release per version tag.</strong> A tag <code>vX.Y.Z</code> builds the library and attaches the
      packed tarball to a GitHub release; apps install that URL (see <a href={url('develop/react/')}>React</a>).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>This site follows main.</strong> It is built from the main branch on every push, so it can describe
      changes that are not in a release yet. The version in its code samples is the latest release.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The file <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> in the repository, rendered here as it is:</p>
  <Changelog />
</Doc>
